    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0235" n="119" xml:id="pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/167.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chairman of the Central Committee of the American National
                            Red Cross.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Receipt is acknowledged of your letter of
                    December 19, 1914, giving the views of the Red Cross on the proposed advance of
                    $5,000,000 on the Huai River loan.</p>
                <p>Pursuant to the suggestion of the Central Committee of the Red Cross, the
                    Department sent a telegram to the American Minister at Peking on December 22,
                    1914, a paraphrase of which is herewith enclosed for your information, setting
                    forth the views of the Committee on the loan.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
